## Confirming your installation

To make sure the WarehousePG software is installed and configured correctly, run the following confirmation steps from your WarehousePG coordinator host. Fix any problems before continuing to the next task.

1.  Log in to the coordinator host as `gpadmin`.

    ```
    su - gpadmin
    ```

2.  Use the `gpssh` utility to check that you can log in to all hosts without a password prompt, and to confirm that the WarehousePG software is installed on all hosts. Use the `hostfile_exkeys` file you used to set up passwordless SSH. For example:

    ```
    gpssh -f hostfile_exkeys -e 'ls -l /usr/local/whpg'
    ```

    If the installation succeeded, you can log in to all hosts without a password prompt. All hosts show the same contents in their installation directories, owned by the `gpadmin` user.

    If you're prompted for a password, run the following command to redo the SSH key exchange.

    ```
    gpssh-exkeys -f hostfile_exkeys
    ```

